# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Large binary artifacts — not version-controlled.
# These are either redistributable third-party software (Docker
# image exports, .deb packages, JDBC drivers) or a packaged archive
# of content already tracked elsewhere in this repo as a directory.
# Regenerate them from the documented build process rather than
# committing them; see README.md and docs/RAH-OIP_Architecture_Proposal.md.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Docker image exports (Portainer, PostgreSQL, SQL Server, etc.)
*.tar

# Curated APT package pool (~500 .deb files, ~377MB) — rebuild via
# the documented apt-get download / dpkg-scanpackages process.
# The package index (Packages) stays small enough to keep; the
# compressed index (Packages.gz) and the .deb payloads do not.
*.deb

# Packaged release archives, e.g. RAH-OIP-1.0.0_Debian13_2026-07-09.zip
# — a zip of content already present and tracked as a directory under
# rah-oip-releases/. Regenerate the archive from that directory.
*.zip

# Third-party JDBC drivers (DBeaver database drivers)
*.jar

# Compressed APT index (derivable from the uncompressed Packages file)
*.gz

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Real credentials for the physical lab environment (VM root/user
# passwords, SSH key paths). Keep local-only, never in git history —
# this is a different risk class than the test-only passwords
# mentioned incidentally in the lessons-learned docs.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
docs/RAH-OIP_LAB_ENVIRONMENT_REFERENCE.md
